   $q$Read the passage: "Lucia loves to bake bread especially on cold Sunday mornings. When the kitchen is quiet. Her brother Ayo helps knead the dough." Which revision corrects every sentence boundary error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lucia loves to bake bread. Especially on cold Sunday mornings. When the kitchen is quiet, her brother Ayo helps knead the dough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-fragment-created"},{"text":"Lucia loves to bake bread, especially on cold Sunday mornings. When the kitchen is quiet. Her brother Ayo helps knead the dough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dependent-clause-fragment-left"},{"text":"Lucia loves to bake bread, especially on cold Sunday mornings when the kitchen is quiet, her brother Ayo helps knead the dough.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"Lucia loves to bake bread, especially on cold Sunday mornings. When the kitchen is quiet, her brother Ayo helps knead the dough.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lucia loves to bake bread, especially on cold Sunday mornings. When the kitchen is quiet, her brother Ayo helps knead the dough.$q$, $q$The "when" clause must attach to "her brother Ayo helps knead the dough" to make a complete sentence. Joining everything with commas fixes the fragment but splices two complete sentences together.$q$, 'draft', null)
